An Operational Amplifier Comparator(or also called voltage comparator) is an open-looped circuit(meaning that the output does not invoke any action in the circuit) that compares an input voltage to a reference voltage and creates a binary output(0 or 1) that tells which of the 2 voltages are higher. Both of these voltages are analog signals, and the reference voltage signal at the other input leg is fixed.

